Q: Error when using Harmony 2: &#39;Harmony&#39; is a namespace but is used like a type A: <p>There is both <code>Harmony</code> the namespace (from <code>MelonLoader</code>) <em>and</em> <code>Harmony</code> the type. It's unfortunate that the <code>MelonLoader</code> authors did that, to be honest... however, there are options to stop it from being a problem:</p>
<p>First option: qualify the usage:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>HarmonyLib.Harmony harmony = new HarmonyLib.Harmony(&quot;com.xbeardeddice.examplemod&quot;);
</code></pre>
<p>This becomes shorter if you use <code>var</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>var harmony = new HarmonyLib.Harmony(&quot;com.xbeardeddice.examplemod&quot;);
</code></pre>
<p>Second option: create an alias:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>using HarmonyClass = global::HarmonyLib.Harmony;
...
HarmonyClass harmony = new HarmonyClass(&quot;com.xbeardeddice.examplemod&quot;);
</code></pre>
